{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThe 0.11.0 release preflight (`make test`) deterministically fails on a host with `scc` or `lizard` installed at `tests/unit/grounding/test_coverage_reconstruction.py::test_full_backend_account_is_present`. The full run produced 10,782 passes and one failure in 37m22s; the focused test reproduces in 26s. The tiny mixed fixture is below the metric threshold, so a present metric tool returns no findings and therefore no metric evidence record. The test incorrectly asserts that the metric backend is always present. Its sibling `test_metric_backend_skip_is_reconstructable` already forces `_METRIC_CANDIDATES` to a missing binary to make the coverage-account scenario host-independent; the full-account test missed the same control.\n\n## Plan\n- Preserve the existing focused failing test as RED evidence on a metric-enabled host.\n- Add the same explicit missing-metric-tool fixture control to `test_full_backend_account_is_present` so the test measures reconstructable skipped coverage rather than ambient PATH contents.\n- Keep production grounding behavior and the evidence schema unchanged; a successful tool run with no threshold match must not be fabricated as a match or abstain.\n- Run the focused coverage-reconstruction file, the grounding unit tier, lint, typecheck, and the full default suite before landing.\n- Land this release blocker through Gerrit before rebasing the 0.11.0 release commit.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The full-backend account test is deterministic whether or not scc/lizard exists on PATH.\n- [x] The test still proves the metric backend appears as visible skipped coverage with reason no_tool.\n- [x] No production source file or evidence outcome semantics change.\n- [x] The focused coverage-reconstruction file passes.\n- [x] The grounding unit tier passes.\n- [x] Lint and typecheck pass.\n- [x] The full default suite passes.\n- [x] The fix lands through Gerrit with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786060906519403001,"uuid":"096a270f-8958-4d1a-937a-e5fdc9d9f929"}